<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		Tauri CLI merges this file into the default Info.plist generated for
		the macOS bundle. Keep this list minimal so we do not collide with
		fields Tauri populates (CFBundleShortVersionString, CFBundleVersion,
		etc).

		NSDocumentsFolderUsageDescription: macOS Sequoia displays this string
		when the app first tries to read ~/Documents/. Without it, the OS
		denies access silently and there is no way to prompt the user for
		re-permission after a TCC reset (which can happen when the codesign
		identity or bundle hash changes between releases). Graphium reads
		notes, wiki, media and skills from ~/Documents/Graphium/ so the
		dialog needs to appear on first launch.

		NSMicrophoneUsageDescription: shown the first time the meeting
		recorder or voice input opens the default input device (cpal).
		Without it macOS terminates the app on microphone access. Both
		only run when the user presses their button; voice input keeps
		the audio in memory and saves nothing.
	-->
	<key>NSDocumentsFolderUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Graphium needs access to the Documents folder to read and write your notes, wiki, media, and skills stored under ~/Documents/Graphium/.</string>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Graphium uses your microphone only when you press record: to record a meeting, whose audio is saved locally under ~/Documents/Graphium/media/, or to speak into a search or chat box, which keeps the audio in memory, turns it into text on this computer, and saves nothing.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
